./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_002517_46d135b6aad4/full_2026_07_06_rec_002517_46d135b6aad4_docling_json_20260812_213057/docling/chunks.json:2522:    "text": "5 Further Analysis\nFigure 6: (a) Distribution of real cells and generated cells. (b) Gene clusters and their associated pathways.\n\nSCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure with panels labeled **(a)** and **(b)**.\n\nPanel **(a)** shows single-cell embedding plots comparing **real** and **generated** cells. The top plot is labeled **“Cell Source”** and overlays two categories: **Real** and **Generated**, with an annotation **“MMD: 0.007”**. Two lower plots are labeled **“Real Cells”** and **“Generated Cells”**. A legend lists cell-type labels including **Basal**, **Dermal Fibroblast**, **Dermal Papilla**, **Endothelial**, **Hair Shaft-cuticle.cortex**, **IRS**, **Infundibulum**, **Isthmus**, **Medulla**, **Mix**, **ORS**, **Spinous**, **TAC-1**, **TAC-2**, and bulge-related CD34+ populations. The visual comparison suggests the generated cell distribution closely matches the real cell distribution in the embedding space.\n\nPanel **(b)** shows a clustered cell embedding with clusters labeled **1–5** in a legend. The clusters are shown as colored point clouds arranged along a horizontal manifold. Text annotations associate regions with biological processes: **immune system, inflammatory response, cell signaling processes**, **leukocyte functions, immune responses**, **immune cell activation and signaling**, **regulation of tissue structure**, and **tissue development**. Small illustrative icons appear near these annotations. The panel appears to interpret cluster-level biological functions across the embedding.\n\nBiological source objects visible or referenced include cell populations from skin or hair follicle contexts, such as basal cells, dermal fibroblasts, dermal papilla, endothelial cells, hair shaft/cuticle/cortex, inner root sheath, infundibulum, isthmus, medulla, outer root sheath, spinous cells, transit-amplifying cells, and CD34+ bulge-associated cells.\n\nThe figure presents a model output comparison between real and generated single-cell data, likely using dimensionality reduction embeddings and a distributional similarity metric, with downstream cluster/function interpretation.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_002517_46d135b6aad4/full_2026_07_06_rec_002517_46d135b6aad4_docling_json_20260812_213057/docling/chunks.json:4658:    "text": "E Additional Results\nFigure 7 complements Figure 5 by displaying the model's robustness to seen and unseen task descriptions under both base battery-half and large battery-full configurations. This demonstrates CHATCELL's essential chat model capability to handle diverse expressions of task descriptions.\nFigure 7: Performance (%) comparison of drug sensitivity prediction using task descriptions seen or unseen during training under base (a) and large (b) settings.\n\nSCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel bar chart figure with panels labeled **(a)** and **(b)**.\n\nPanel structure:\n- **(a)** contains two horizontal bar charts:\n  - Left: dataset **GSE149383**\n  - Right: dataset **GSE117872**\n- **(b)** contains two horizontal bar charts:\n  - Left: dataset **GSE149383**\n  - Right: dataset **GSE117872**\n\nLegend:\n- Pink bars: **Seen task descriptions**\n- Blue bars: **Unseen task descriptions**\n\nMetrics shown on the y-axis:\n- **Recall**\n- **Precision**\n- **F1**\n- **Acc**\n\nVisible findings:\n- In panel **(a)**, GSE149383 scores are around **95.27–95.68**, with unseen task descriptions slightly higher than seen for several metrics.\n- In panel **(a)**, GSE117872 scores are around **97.71–98.49**, with seen and unseen values appearing identical or nearly identical for each metric.\n- In panel **(b)**, GSE149383 scores are around **97.09–97.83**, with seen task descriptions higher than unseen.\n- In panel **(b)**, GSE117872 scores are around **98.46–99.24**, with seen task descriptions higher than unseen.\n\nBiological/source objects:\n- The only visible biological identifiers are dataset names **GSE149383** and **GSE117872**, which appear to be GEO accession IDs. No cells, tissues, genes, microscopy images, or molecular structures are visible.\n\nTransformations/model interfaces:\n- The figure compares model performance under **seen vs unseen task descriptions** using classification metrics. No model architecture, pipeline, embedding, or interface diagram is shown.\nMeanwhile, Figure 8 provides a detailed expansion of Figure 6 (b), showing each gene cluster and its most associated pathways. This proves CHATCELL's ability to capture the relationships between genes and their functions, thereby enhancing its comprehension of biological processes.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_06/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001343_6968c1123911/full_2026_07_06_rec_001343_6968c1123911_docling_json_20260812_194019/docling_graph/graph.html:1733:        "supporting_figure_or_table": "Figure 6; Figure 7; Table 6",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_06/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001343_6968c1123911/full_2026_07_06_rec_001343_6968c1123911_docling_json_20260812_194019/docling_graph/graph.html:1799:        "supporting_figure_or_table": "Table 6; Figure 6; Figure 7",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6/full_2026_07_06_rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6_docling_json_20260812_193428/docling_graph/graph.html:9606:        "route_label": "Figure 6",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6/full_2026_07_06_rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6_docling_json_20260812_193428/docling_graph/graph.html:9628:        "supporting_figure_or_table": "Figure 6",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6/full_2026_07_06_rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6_docling_json_20260812_193428/debug/dense_provenance.json:2464:      "text": "4. Experiments\n4.5. Interpretability Analysis\nWe probe model interpretability with Grad-CAM on the multi-page fusion representations (see Appendix K.7 for implementation details). Fig. 4 visualizes two pages from a donor-labeled Japonica test document. Unlike sequencebased models that distribute attention diffusely at the base level, OpticalDNA produces localized attributions over short contiguous regions, reflecting region-level processing induced by visual tokenization and local receptive fields. This phrase-like reading behavior mirrors how humans process long text and is particularly well suited for long DNA documents, as it avoids exhaustive base-wise scanning while preserving informative local patterns under a fixed token budget. Importantly, Grad-CAM activations concentrate around the annotated donor splice site (purple box), and the corresponding page receives higher overall attribution, indicating that OpticalDNA can both localize biologically meaningful splice signals and prioritize the most relevant pages during inference. Overall, these results indicate that OpticalDNA learns structured, region-aware representations aligned with genomic reasoning, while also offering practical interpretability, highlighting its potential utility for large-scale genomic and transcriptomic analyses.\nTable 6. ROI identification on T2 (IoU = 0 . 99 ).\n\nOpticalDNA-HG38, LCM \u2191 = 0.9871. OpticalDNA-HG38, Joint \u2191 = 0.9820. OpticalDNA-HG38, Strict \u2191 = 0.8763. OpticalDNA-HG38, \u2113 \u221e \u2193 = 0.3941. OpticalDNA-Rice, LCM \u2191 = 0.9991. OpticalDNA-Rice, Joint \u2191 = 0.9692. OpticalDNA-Rice, Strict \u2191 = 0.8084. OpticalDNA-Rice, \u2113 \u221e \u2193 = 0.3243\nAbbrev. LCM: line-count match; Joint: line-level joint accuracy (text+ROI); Strict: page-level strict success.\nFigure 4. Grad-CAM visualization on multi-page fusion for a donor case (two pages). Purple boxes indicate donor splice sites; numbers denote page-level mean attribution.\n\nSCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image shows two side-by-side text panels containing dense nucleotide/DNA-like sequences highlighted in green. Each panel appears to be a page or sequence block comparison view.\n\nVisible elements:\n- Left panel labeled `Page#0: 0.530`\n- Right panel labeled `Page#4: 0.585`\n- A horizontal color/score bar at the bottom ranging from `0` to `1`, with midpoint `0.5`\n- Most sequence text is shaded green, suggesting a continuous heatmap or confidence/similarity overlay\n- A vertical divider separates the two panels\n\nBiological source objects:\n- DNA/RNA nucleotide strings composed primarily of A, C, G, and T characters\n\nLikely transformation/interface:\n- Sequence text has been rendered as page images and overlaid with a green intensity map, possibly representing similarity, attribution, relevance, or matching score.\n- The page-level numeric labels may indicate scores for each extracted page/panel.\n\nVisible finding:\n- Both panels contain strong green-highlighted sequence regions, with the right panel having a slightly higher displayed score (`0.585`) than the left (`0.530`).",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_05/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6/full_2026_07_06_rec_001830_eb50f2bf58e6_docling_json_20260812_193428/debug/dense_provenance.json:2696:      "text": "4. Experiments\n4.7. Rendering Robustness\nFigure 6. Low-resolution robustness on the Adipose Subcutaneous eQTL task. AUROC remains stable under moderate downsampling and degrades mainly at extreme resolutions.\n\nSCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nSingle line chart showing model performance across image downsampling resolutions.\n\nVisible elements:\n- X-axis: \u201cDownsampled resolution\u201d with labels `64\u00d764`, `128\u00d7128`, `256\u00d7256`, `320\u00d7320`, `640\u00d7640`.\n- Y-axis: \u201cAUROC\u201d, ranging roughly from `0.76` to `0.84`.\n- Green line with circular markers connects AUROC values:\n  - `64\u00d764`: `0.768`\n  - `128\u00d7128`: `0.799`\n  - `256\u00d7256`: `0.812`\n  - `320\u00d7320`: `0.828`\n  - `640\u00d7640`: `0.813`\n- Dashed horizontal reference line labeled \u201cNative 640\u00d7640\u201d near AUROC `0.812`.\n- Finding: AUROC improves from low resolution to `320\u00d7320`, peaks at `0.828`, then decreases slightly at `640\u00d7640` to `0.813`, close to the native-resolution reference line.\n\nNo biological source objects, microscopy images, anatomical structures, transformations, or model interface diagrams are visible in this extracted image.",
