./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_06/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001838_bb6ae63f17ad/full_2026_07_06_rec_001838_bb6ae63f17ad_docling_json_20260812_200246/docling/document.json:5929:      "orig": "Figure 6 shows a skewed distribution of the top 30 tissue categories (out of 347), with brain (211,063) and blood (177,460) leading, likely due to extensive sampling in neurological and hematological research. Tissues like lung (87,784) and eye (59,430) follow, reflecting biases toward accessible or clinically relevant sources.",
./data/living_catalog/taxonomy_rerun_preflight_2026-08-12/taxonomy/runs/classification_dense/shard_06/records/full_2026-07-06__rec_001838_bb6ae63f17ad/full_2026_07_06_rec_001838_bb6ae63f17ad_docling_json_20260812_200246/docling/document.json:5930:      "text": "Figure 6 shows a skewed distribution of the top 30 tissue categories (out of 347), with brain (211,063) and blood (177,460) leading, likely due to extensive sampling in neurological and hematological research. Tissues like lung (87,784) and eye (59,430) follow, reflecting biases toward accessible or clinically relevant sources."
